{"ts": 1789709010.6212611, "kind": "assistant_text", "text": "## Summary\n\nI explored the feature space systematically:\n\n1. **Single-feature scan**: Evaluated all 40 features individually (with sign chosen to maximize Sharpe). Feature 13 stood out clearly with an in-sample Sharpe of **0.755**, well above the next best (F35 at 0.625, F38 at 0.489).\n\n2. **Combination search**: Tried ~50 two- and three-feature combinations pairing F13 (and other top performers like F35, F38, F4, F19) with each other and with mid-tier features. Notably, **every combination involving F13 performed worse than F13 alone** \u2014 often substantially worse, sometimes even flipping sign \u2014 suggesting F13 captures a distinct, fairly clean signal that other features mostly dilute or conflict with rather than complement.\n\n3. **Robustness check**: Tested combos among the other top singles (F35, F38, F4, F19, F18, F14) \u2014 best of these topped out around 0.47-0.48, still below plain F13.\n\n**Final specification**: Feature 13, long, alone (up to 3 features allowed, but 1 was best).\n\n**Predicted OOS Sharpe**: mean = 0.4, sd = 0.3 \u2014 I discounted meaningfully from the in-sample 0.755 because this was the best of 40 single-feature draws plus ~50 combination tests, so some in-sample outperformance is likely due to selection/multiple-comparisons rather than pure signal, even though the margin over the second-best feature was large enough to suggest real signal survives out of sample."}
